    "body": "## P1 privacy/security hardening\n\nThe notification inbox, unread count, read-state mutations and realtime-preference operations accepted a null or transient principal and passed it into private notification persistence. HTTP security should normally supply a persisted principal, but the service boundary must fail closed independently instead of relying on repository behavior or persistence errors.\n\n## Change\n\n- require an authenticated principal with a persisted user id before every user-facing notification read or mutation;\n- validate identity before pagination construction, repository access or preference validation/mutation;\n- keep internal notification creation behavior and realtime delivery ordering unchanged;\n- bring the notification documentation in sync with the existing `SAVED_SEARCH_MATCH` preference and record the identity invariant.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nA focused test exercises null and transient principals across inbox listing, unread count, preference read/write, single read-state mutation and bulk read-state mutation, and proves zero notification/preference/realtime interactions occur.\n\n## Roadmap\n\nAdvances the endpoint-by-endpoint authorization and private-state audit (#615, #618, #620; umbrella #957).\n\n## Merge gate\n\nBranch is based on green `master` `e23672b3cdf2892cd4461d2c55d316a6755b4ca5` after PR #229. Merge only after every relevant workflow is green on the exact current PR head `83da9f70ff0810ada14187b31367c830479fc8df`, review threads are clear, and `master` is revalidated immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it safely and rerun the exact-head gate. Merge commit only.",
